rota lap 4265, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; its fixed seat is witness before narrative and its fusion strand is a guard that cannot red guards nothing, which is the lens the shared-pen guard was read under
think Cold open refused twice before it ran -- the first pass produced no receipt and the second met run_lock=in_flight pid 2001031, which resolved through /proc to THIS tree, so the pass I thought had died was my own still running. I had waited on the wrong pid (769271, cwd unresolved, started twelve minutes earlier). Waiting on a pid read from the lock file rather than from a ps grep is the habit that lap taught.
think The aether row read against the card's open remainders: %601 asks for a guard reading tracked runners for a fixed /tmp/<name> write, and one was already standing -- tools/fixtures/s/shared_pen_scan.sh. Reading its WHY beside its source line is what found the fault: the WHY says eight checkouts share one /tmp, which names no directory, and the source line said git ls-files 'tools/*'.
think Measured the gap before repairing it: 68 tracked .sh and .rish outside tools/, and the roster already RUNS that room -- tools/r/rish_join_split_witness.rish runs three scripts under rishi/tests/ and tools/fixtures/r/rishi_bounded_process_control.sh runs six more. So the blind spot was reachable rather than theoretical.
think Widened the source line to every tracked .sh and .rish, 3,221 to 3,289 sources. vendor/ and gratitude/ are gitlinks so no vendored byte enters. The widening found exactly one file -- rishi/tests/file_io.rish, five sites, no wipe -- whose own rostered sibling tools/r/rish_file_io_witness.rish had written into the gitignored anchor tools/fixtures/rish_io/ since it was seated. The elder copy never followed and nothing could say so.
think Repaired the file to that anchor and ran it GREEN on metal, so both ceilings stay where they stood: 236 sites, 46 files, 15 wiping, measured tools/-only before the widening and widened-plus-repaired after. Reach bought, number unchanged -- the one shape a population widening can take without asking for slack.
think Three control legs, each proven from both sides: the same token planted under tools/ and outside it must BOTH count, and a date/ shelf outside tools/ must still pass free -- an exemption proven in one room only cannot be told from an accident. behaviors 41 -> 44, faults 0.
obs A population selected by directory is a choice wearing a rule's clothes, and it reads as coverage from every side. This is %532's hand-written enumeration one instrument over, spelled as a glob rather than a list. The tell is cheap and general: read a guard's own WHY paragraph and ask whether it names the boundary its source line draws.
obs The card opened with seven bytes free, so the account could not be written until the elder block folded. That is the standing bill rather than this lap's fault; the cairn records it and names the four bytes the next ship will meet.
obs What this lap does NOT reach is %601's real remainder -- a lap's own typed /tmp name lives in no file, so no reading of tracked sources can see it. Named on the card as a question rather than answered.
